WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.249
Most outreach fails in predictable patterns.

00:00:02.249 --> 00:00:04.123
Learn to spot them fast.

00:00:04.123 --> 00:00:06.747
This lesson is about live critique patterns.

00:00:06.747 --> 00:00:07.872
What usually fails.

00:00:07.872 --> 00:00:10.496
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.496 --> 00:00:14.244
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.244 --> 00:00:19.867
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:23.990
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.488
Stay practical: spot three failure patterns before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.808 --> 00:00:33.492
Three common failures: no clear ask, pitching before discovery, and zero follow-up.

00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:36.224
Remember the objective: spot three failure patterns.

00:00:36.224 --> 00:00:40.517
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:45.201
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.201 --> 00:00:49.495
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.495 --> 00:00:54.179
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:56.911
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.911 --> 00:00:58.472
Feedback beats guessing alone.

